</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 428)</h2>
<p><b>Open a delivery folder, double-click a session — both just work.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Opening a folder now handles everything inside it: a folder of QuickTimes, an image sequence, or a whole vendor tree with sequences and movies in subfolders — all of it becomes the playlist. A chip shows scanning progress, and only a genuinely huge haul (60+ clips or 25 GB) asks before opening.</li>
<li>Double-clicking a saved session (or invite, or license) in Finder now opens it properly — previously it launched a blank window.</li>
<li>Fixed a race where a session opened into a fresh window showed its clips in the filmstrip but a black picture at 0% zoom.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
